1. Definitions

"Software" means this source code, its documentation, and any modified
version or derivative work of them that is distributed under this License.
Software does not include third-party components, which remain subject to
their own licenses.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
License. If You accept on behalf of an entity, You represent that You have
authority to bind it.

"Commercial Use" means using, modifying, distributing, hosting, or making
the Software available in connection with a business or other activity
intended primarily for commercial advantage or monetary compensation.
Examples include selling or licensing the Software; offering it as a paid
product, hosted service, or subscription; using it to provide paid services;
and monetizing products or content generated with it. Internal business use
is Commercial Use even if it does not itself generate separately identifiable
revenue.

"Gross Revenue" means all amounts invoiced, earned, or received by You or
Your affiliates from Commercial Use of the Software, including sales,
subscriptions, license fees, service fees, advertising, sponsorships, and
other monetization. For a bundle or combined offering, Gross Revenue includes
the portion reasonably attributable to the Software, determined in good
faith using a consistent allocation method. Gross Revenue excludes sales,
value-added, and similar transaction taxes collected for and remitted to a
government, and amounts actually refunded to customers or charged back.

"Licensor" means the copyright holder(s) of the Software who offer this
License.

2. Non-commercial permission

Subject to this License, Licensor grants You a worldwide, non-exclusive,
royalty-free, non-transferable license to use, reproduce, modify, and
distribute the Software for personal, educational, research, evaluation, and
other non-commercial purposes.

When You distribute the Software or a modified version for a non-commercial
purpose, You must:

  a. include this License and preserve applicable copyright and attribution
     notices;
  b. identify files You have modified; and
  c. license the Software and those modifications under this License.

You may not remove or alter this License's commercial-use and revenue-share
requirements.

3. Commercial use and revenue share

The permission in Section 2 does not authorize Commercial Use. Commercial
Use is permitted only while You comply with all of the following conditions:

  a. You owe Licensor a revenue share equal to ten percent (10%) of Gross
     Revenue for each calendar quarter in which You make Commercial Use;
  b. within thirty (30) days after the end of each calendar quarter, You
     provide Licensor a written report stating the Gross Revenue calculation
     and pay the corresponding revenue share. If Gross Revenue is zero, You
     must still submit a zero-revenue report;
  c. You keep complete records reasonably sufficient to verify each report
     for at least three (3) years and, on reasonable written notice no more
     than once per year, allow Licensor or an independent auditor bound by
     confidentiality to inspect those records. An underpayment exceeding
     five percent (5%) for an audited period must be promptly paid, together
     with reasonable audit costs; and
  d. You contact Licensor before beginning Commercial Use to agree in writing
     on payment details and a reporting contact. This administrative step
     does not change the ten percent share or quarterly deadlines.

If You cannot or do not agree to these conditions, You must not make
Commercial Use of the Software. Licensor may offer a separate written
commercial license; no such license is granted unless signed by Licensor.

